<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan beef imports down 17.8 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan beef imports down 17.8 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in January were down 17.8 percent at 40,514 tonnes from the same period a year earlier, according to data released by the Finance Ministry on Friday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Jan 97	 Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p> Total	    40,514	 48,458     49,272</p>
<p> Refrigerated   20,977	 28,008     24,080</p>
<p> Frozen	   19,537	 19,923     25,192</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     11,684	 15,739     13,836</p>
<p>  U.S.	     8,651	 11,394	9,500</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Jan 97	 Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p> U.S.		9,700	 10,701	16,105</p>
<p> Australia	 7,832	  7,454	 9,179</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in calendar 1996 were 320,855 tonnes against 364,250 tonnes a year earlier. Frozen beef imports in 1996 were 308,774 tonnes against 221,807 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7531</p>
</text>
